  2. Current AreaVersion Schema and Behavior

  V2__core_schema.sql — area_version table:

  CREATE TABLE area_version (
      id          UUID                   NOT NULL,  -- PK
      area_id     UUID                   NOT NULL,  -- FK → area
      version     INTEGER                NOT NULL,
      name        VARCHAR(255)           NOT NULL,
      geometry    geometry(POLYGON, 4326) NOT NULL,
      area_km2    NUMERIC(20, 6)         NOT NULL,
      status      VARCHAR(50)            NOT NULL,  -- 'ACTIVE' | 'DELETED'
      change_type VARCHAR(50)            NOT NULL,  -- 'CREATED' | 'UPDATED' | 'DELETED' | 'RESTORED'
      created_by  UUID                   NOT NULL,  -- FK → users
      created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ            NOT NULL,
      UNIQUE (area_id, version)
  );

  Java entity (AreaVersion.java): exposes id, area (lazy FK), version, name, geometry, areaKm2, status, changeType, createdBy (lazy FK → User), createdAt.

  AreaVersionResponse DTO (API-visible): id, version, name, geometry, areaKm2, status, changeType, createdBy (UUID), createdAt.

  AreaService behavior (verified in code):
  - createArea passes createdByUserId and writes ChangeType.CREATED in the same @Transactional method.
  - updateArea passes updatedByUserId and writes ChangeType.UPDATED transactionally.
  - deleteArea passes deletedByUserId and writes ChangeType.DELETED transactionally.
  - restoreArea passes restoredByUserId and writes ChangeType.RESTORED transactionally.

  All four mutation flows: Area write + AreaVersion insert are atomic in a single @Transactional method. @TransactionalEventListener(AFTER_COMMIT) ensures the WebSocket event fires only after commit.

  The workspace association is one join away: area_version.area_id → area.workspace_id. workspace_id is not directly stored on area_version.

